## Findings

1. blocking — brief:48 — The agent-written interpretation of “the route label truncates first” clips `Opens Board drawer` even when both fields fit. The fixed 112px cap unnecessarily obscures the destination in inbox-sample-1280.png and inbox-board-only-840.png. — replace with: “The route label yields to the ask kinds, truncating only when the ask kinds would otherwise not fit, and shows `Opens Board drawer` in full whenever both fit.” Remove the fixed `.inbox__route` cap. — check: w025.css; Board-owned Inbox rows at 1280, 840, 640 and 390.
2. advisory — brief:19 — The revised Intent omits ownership and scope statements still retained elsewhere in the brief; restoring them makes the summary complete without changing the design. — replace with: Append “A row with an Inbox decision keeps its existing detail and answer controls in Inbox, and a combined row exposes a small `Open Board actions` control. The Board strip uses the same ownership: replyable questions open their Inbox detail, while Board-only asks reuse the lifecycle-card drawer. No public deep route, second count, endpoint, write shape or drawer is added.” — check: studio/briefs/W-487.md:19 against lines 48, 50, 106–107.

